(545478, 54165, 3080, '<td valign="top">Definately a good point of view, which I supose is what this challenge is all about.  However, while the POINT OF VIEW is good...the view itself doesn''t really appeal to me.  It''s just a personal opinion, and nothing against the technical aspects of this shot, which are good, but I''m just not drawn into the shot.  The one suggestion that I may have though is that the focus seems to be on the mouse butt.  Not the best part of the photo in my opinion.  Would like to see the cat face in focus instead.  The lighting is good, as is the cropping and framing.  ~Heather~</td>', 'Definately a good point of view, which I supose is what this challenge is all about.  However, while the POINT OF VIEW is good...the view itself doesn''t really appeal to me.  It''s just a personal opinion, and nothing against the technical aspects of this shot, which are good, but I''m just not drawn into the shot.  The one suggestion that I may have though is that the focus seems to be on the mouse butt.  Not the best part of the photo in my opinion.  Would like to see the cat face in focus instead.  The lighting is good, as is the cropping and framing.  ~Heather~', '2004-01-16 01:23:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(545479, 54841, 3080, '<td valign="top">I guess this could be considered a point of view.  My first thought is that point of view is the WAY you LOOK at something, not HOW you SEE something.  Very similar, but very different.  Either way, this shot doesn''t appeal to me in any way.  I''m not really finding a point of interest, nor a focal point to rest my eyes on.  There isn''t really a subject.  The darkness obviously triggered a slow shutter speed and I don''t think this is an appropriate use of the slow shutter speed.   Just not my thing.  ~Heather~</td>', 'I guess this could be considered a point of view.  My first thought is that point of view is the WAY you LOOK at something, not HOW you SEE something.  Very similar, but very different.  Either way, this shot doesn''t appeal to me in any way.  I''m not really finding a point of interest, nor a focal point to rest my eyes on.  There isn''t really a subject.  The darkness obviously triggered a slow shutter speed and I don''t think this is an appropriate use of the slow shutter speed.   Just not my thing.  ~Heather~', '2004-01-16 01:30:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(545480, 54483, 3080, '<td valign="top">Would look good in the "inside looking out" challenge too.  You did a wonderful job of making the glass in focus.  clarity is really good.  I''m wondering though if there might be just a tad too much of the container in the shot.  I want to say that I wish there were less container, but then if there were, would we still be able to tell what was going on in the shot?  I''d have to see it to make the judgement.  But something to think about anyway.  the lighting on the glass is really good.  and refreshing looking for sure.  a good idea for the challenge. ~Heather~</td>', 'Would look good in the "inside looking out" challenge too.  You did a wonderful job of making the glass in focus.  clarity is really good.  I''m wondering though if there might be just a tad too much of the container in the shot.  I want to say that I wish there were less container, but then if there were, would we still be able to tell what was going on in the shot?  I''d have to see it to make the judgement.  But something to think about anyway.  the lighting on the glass is really good.  and refreshing looking for sure.  a good idea for the challenge. ~Heather~', '2004-01-16 01:33:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(545481, 54957, 3080, '<td valign="top">I like the DOF on this shot.  Very nice focus and clarity.  The lighting is good as well.  The subject isn''t something I''d personally hang on my wall, but this is technically good non the less.  I like the angle and the POV makes this interesting to look at.  That''s what the challenge is about.  ~Heather~</td>', 'I like the DOF on this shot.  Very nice focus and clarity.  The lighting is good as well.  The subject isn''t something I''d personally hang on my wall, but this is technically good non the less.  I like the angle and the POV makes this interesting to look at.  That''s what the challenge is about.  ~Heather~', '2004-01-16 01:36:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(545482, 54926, 9027, '<td valign="top">nice....down with cigarettes! haha. only thing bothersome is that plastic thing on the bottom of the carton. what is that?</td>', 'nice....down with cigarettes! haha. only thing bothersome is that plastic thing on the bottom of the carton. what is that?', '2004-01-16 01:38:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(545483, 54778, 9027, '<td valign="top">i think this would have made a more interesting b/w photo. the colors aren''t very strong in the color and the bw would bring out the cool shapes inthe bent metal.</td>', 'i think this would have made a more interesting b/w photo. the colors aren''t very strong in the color and the bw would bring out the cool shapes inthe bent metal.', '2004-01-16 01:40:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(545484, 54808, 3080, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately being on SC I had the opportunity to view the original color version of this shot when proof was requested.  I have to say I liked the color version better, but don''t know if I would have even considered it had I not SEEN the color version.  If that makes sense.  I like the lines, like the curves, and the pov is interesting.  not sure how I feel about the sun beams.  They don''t seem to follow the angle of the POV, which draws my eyes away from that a bit.  Overall though, I think it''s a very nice image.  ~Heather~</td>', 'Unfortunately being on SC I had the opportunity to view the original color version of this shot when proof was requested.  I have to say I liked the color version better, but don''t know if I would have even considered it had I not SEEN the color version.  If that makes sense.  I like the lines, like the curves, and the pov is interesting.  not sure how I feel about the sun beams.  They don''t seem to follow the angle of the POV, which draws my eyes away from that a bit.  Overall though, I think it''s a very nice image.  ~Heather~', '2004-01-16 01:41:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(545485, 54777, 9027, '<td valign="top">nicely composed. i like the foreshortening and dramatic perspective.</td>', 'nicely composed. i like the foreshortening and dramatic perspective.', '2004-01-16 01:41:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(545487, 55119, 9027, '<td valign="top">nice perspective. the choice of color, makes this haunting.</td>', 'nice perspective. the choice of color, makes this haunting.', '2004-01-16 01:45:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(545488, 54333, 3080, '<td valign="top">your little chickadee is cute, but i''m not seeing how the point of view makes this any more interesting.  the background looks a bit grainy, and the dark bottom left corner is a bit of a distraction to the bird.  I like the blue tint over the image.  There is the strong impression of coldness in this shot, and that is good.  I like strong impressions.  Focus and clarity are good...just not really seeing an interesting point of view.  not the kind I have pictured in my own head anyway.  still a nice image though. ~Heather~</td>', 'your little chickadee is cute, but i''m not seeing how the point of view makes this any more interesting.  the background looks a bit grainy, and the dark bottom left corner is a bit of a distraction to the bird.  I like the blue tint over the image.  There is the strong impression of coldness in this shot, and that is good.  I like strong impressions.  Focus and clarity are good...just not really seeing an interesting point of view.  not the kind I have pictured in my own head anyway.  still a nice image though. ~Heather~', '2004-01-16 01:45:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(545489, 54807, 9027, '<td valign="top">very cool image. love the lines and shapes in it. border adds a nice touch.</td>', 'very cool image. love the lines and shapes in it. border adds a nice touch.', '2004-01-16 01:46:11.000000', NULL, 1),
