(549688, 54931, 4007, '<td valign="top">The two shapes complement each other very nicely, although I do wish the whole thing were in sharper focus.</td>', 'The two shapes complement each other very nicely, although I do wish the whole thing were in sharper focus.', '2004-01-19 22:35:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(549692, 54381, 4007, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure exactly why, but I absolutely love this shot.  The placement of the cassette is great, and the tape is strewn with a wonderful random flair, going in and out of the frame and forming all sorts of twists and loops and such.  A great creative idea executed beautifully.  I hope this ribbons.</td>', 'I''m not sure exactly why, but I absolutely love this shot.  The placement of the cassette is great, and the tape is strewn with a wonderful random flair, going in and out of the frame and forming all sorts of twists and loops and such.  A great creative idea executed beautifully.  I hope this ribbons.', '2004-01-19 22:37:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(549695, 54173, 4007, '<td valign="top">A very interesting point of view indeed.  Very creative idea and executed nicely.  A bit more contrast would help this out I think, as the pale look doesn''t work well for me.</td>', 'A very interesting point of view indeed.  Very creative idea and executed nicely.  A bit more contrast would help this out I think, as the pale look doesn''t work well for me.', '2004-01-19 22:38:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(549708, 54751, 5822, '<td valign="top">Not sure why you would have the lettering backwards as this is quite distracting. Pretty neat image though. Can''t wait to find out how it was done.</td>', 'Not sure why you would have the lettering backwards as this is quite distracting. Pretty neat image though. Can''t wait to find out how it was done.', '2004-01-19 22:49:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(549722, 54932, 7778, '<td valign="top">The wonderful naive illusion created here is rare, to say the least. <br/>On first sight, the image appears to be one coming out of a box of crayons, if not straight out of a fairy tale. On closer examination, the apparent -flat- feel, however, yields considerable depth. When we resist the decoy of the elaborate lattice work of twigs and branches obscuring a clear view of the ground, the trunks of trees become visible alongside numerous tufts of fern fringing a winding path (?). <br/>Since no texture is given anywhere on its course, an allegory of a creek or brook is equally established, while the apparent birds'' eye perspective is quite incidentally concealed by the proximity of the wicker work.<br/> <br/>The magic of this capture, IMO, derives from a rift between the impression of an immediately obvious naivity on hand hand and the complexities obsctructing such a view on the other. The extreme point of view, it seems, makes full use of its vantage and has, I feel, laid out a picture which appears to have composed itself. The undulating -snake-, I discovered, leads the viewer precisely in, through and out of the image. <br/> <br/>Straining to add something negative, I''d wish for a little less of some very light greys and  blown highlights in and along the twigs and branches. How to accomplish this, without effecting that which I cannot fault, is something this image has made me forget. ;-)<br/> <br/>&gt; 9</td>', 'The wonderful naive illusion created here is rare, to say the least. On first sight, the image appears to be one coming out of a box of crayons, if not straight out of a fairy tale. On closer examination, the apparent -flat- feel, however, yields considerable depth. When we resist the decoy of the elaborate lattice work of twigs and branches obscuring a clear view of the ground, the trunks of trees become visible alongside numerous tufts of fern fringing a winding path (?). Since no texture is given anywhere on its course, an allegory of a creek or brook is equally established, while the apparent birds'' eye perspective is quite incidentally concealed by the proximity of the wicker work. The magic of this capture, IMO, derives from a rift between the impression of an immediately obvious naivity on hand hand and the complexities obsctructing such a view on the other. The extreme point of view, it seems, makes full use of its vantage and has, I feel, laid out a picture which appears to have composed itself. The undulating -snake-, I discovered, leads the viewer precisely in, through and out of the image.  Straining to add something negative, I''d wish for a little less of some very light greys and  blown highlights in and along the twigs and branches. How to accomplish this, without effecting that which I cannot fault, is something this image has made me forget. ;-) > 9', '2004-01-19 23:00:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(549726, 54567, 3540, '<td valign="top">Noisy sky.  I''ve looked at this photo 3 times before I actually levied a vote.  I think it looks a lot like a layered photo.   It doesn''t look very natural.  I think the subject is pretty good and it is well framed.  The brush kind of breaks up some of the monotony on the left side, but it almost seems it doesn''t belong there.</td>', 'Noisy sky.  I''ve looked at this photo 3 times before I actually levied a vote.  I think it looks a lot like a layered photo.   It doesn''t look very natural.  I think the subject is pretty good and it is well framed.  The brush kind of breaks up some of the monotony on the left side, but it almost seems it doesn''t belong there.', '2004-01-19 23:03:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(549744, 54454, 13305, '<td valign="top">Good idea, but the flash is too harsh and overexposed the outer part of the photo. Try a diffuser if you have to use the onboard flash.</td>', 'Good idea, but the flash is too harsh and overexposed the outer part of the photo. Try a diffuser if you have to use the onboard flash.', '2004-01-19 23:15:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(549745, 54289, 5822, '<td valign="top">Even with the excessive noise, this is an awesome shot. Very moody and with a very unusual structure.  Lighting is strage in that the snow bank in the lower left is brighter than the rest of the image.  You can clean up the noise problem with Neat Image.  Good luck.</td>', 'Even with the excessive noise, this is an awesome shot. Very moody and with a very unusual structure.  Lighting is strage in that the snow bank in the lower left is brighter than the rest of the image.  You can clean up the noise problem with Neat Image.  Good luck.', '2004-01-19 23:15:57.000000', NULL, 1),
