(551214, 54866, 7252, '<td valign="top">This was one of the few I voted a 10. I''m surprised it wasn''t much higher in the rankings. Creative, well exposed, sharp. Overall very well done.</td>', 'This was one of the few I voted a 10. I''m surprised it wasn''t much higher in the rankings. Creative, well exposed, sharp. Overall very well done.', '2004-01-21 00:37:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(551220, 54215, 2373, '<td valign="top">I used the canon 75-300 usmIII . I love this lense. It is an excellent value for the money. If you could spend just a little more you could get the same one with an  image stabilizer. Oh ya.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-01-25 01:05:26.</i></td>', 'I used the canon 75-300 usmIII . I love this lense. It is an excellent value for the money. If you could spend just a little more you could get the same one with an  image stabilizer. Oh ya.', '2004-01-21 00:40:04.000000', '2004-01-25 01:05:26.000000', 0),
(551222, 54664, 14043, '<td valign="top">Oh man, missed a 5 by .004 points.  :(<br/> <br/>Yes, I realized that "obscured" didn''t work until just after the voting began, it should have been "undefined" like <b>Pepette</b> said.  And the picture was rather boring, hence why I chose the one with the extreme DOF.  The title did factor a lot into making it interesting, that''s what I was going for.<br/> <br/>Yay, <b>JamieWillmott</b> noticed the tiled horizon!  The leading lines in that were just too cool to pass up.<br/> <br/>Hahaha!  <b>ChrisW123</b>- I was going to enter one taken at the same time with the title: "Through the Eyes of My Dog"<br/> <br/>I should have probably put something into the foreground to pull some interest, but I was on a limited schedule and it didn''t occur to me.  Not to mention I felt a bit silly for putting my camera down on the ground in the middle of a shopping center.  ^_^<br/> <br/>Thanks everyone for taking the time to comment and vote!  And you too, <b>bruchen</b>!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-01-21 00:42:28.</i></td>', 'Oh man, missed a 5 by .004 points.  :( Yes, I realized that "obscured" didn''t work until just after the voting began, it should have been "undefined" like Pepette said.  And the picture was rather boring, hence why I chose the one with the extreme DOF.  The title did factor a lot into making it interesting, that''s what I was going for. Yay, JamieWillmott noticed the tiled horizon!  The leading lines in that were just too cool to pass up. Hahaha!  ChrisW123- I was going to enter one taken at the same time with the title: "Through the Eyes of My Dog" I should have probably put something into the foreground to pull some interest, but I was on a limited schedule and it didn''t occur to me.  Not to mention I felt a bit silly for putting my camera down on the ground in the middle of a shopping center.  ^_^ Thanks everyone for taking the time to comment and vote!  And you too, bruchen!!', '2004-01-21 00:41:01.000000', '2004-01-21 00:42:28.000000', 0),
