(553275, 54393, 14773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jaguar:</b></div><hr/><i>Is this your little brother? If so, then we really aren''t looking through his eyes. If you had something he was doing that reflected him and what meant to be dramatic, that would really produce a strong impression.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>when you think of it that way, the title is off, but the expression is what the photographer was referring to..it''s a bit of an exasperated look.  I like it.</td>', 'Originally posted by Jaguar:Is this your little brother? If so, then we really aren''t looking through his eyes. If you had something he was doing that reflected him and what meant to be dramatic, that would really produce a strong impression.  when you think of it that way, the title is off, but the expression is what the photographer was referring to..it''s a bit of an exasperated look.  I like it.', '2004-01-22 10:32:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(553290, 54205, 12151, '<td valign="top">I disagree; if you look at the score distribution, the really high scores and the really low scores are about even in number, and they cancel.  The majority of voters gave this a medium score.  I don''t think this is a great shot technically, and that''s why it got voted down.  The whole "violence" factor does make one wonder what the purpose of the photo is... I personally still don''t "get it"; and if there''s nothing to get - if I''m just supposed to appreciate it for what it is, I can''t, because it just doesn''t look appealing to me technically. <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beagleboy:</b></div><hr/><i>Another instance where this should have scored much higher.  You got trashed by the anti-violence, anti-reality crew.  You focussed this perfectly: the victim in soft focus takes away the over-the-top gore factor that we see in police file shots.  Keep up the good work.</i></td></tr></table></td>', 'I disagree; if you look at the score distribution, the really high scores and the really low scores are about even in number, and they cancel.  The majority of voters gave this a medium score.  I don''t think this is a great shot technically, and that''s why it got voted down.  The whole "violence" factor does make one wonder what the purpose of the photo is... I personally still don''t "get it"; and if there''s nothing to get - if I''m just supposed to appreciate it for what it is, I can''t, because it just doesn''t look appealing to me technically.  Originally posted by Beagleboy:Another instance where this should have scored much higher.  You got trashed by the anti-violence, anti-reality crew.  You focussed this perfectly: the victim in soft focus takes away the over-the-top gore factor that we see in police file shots.  Keep up the good work.', '2004-01-22 10:56:21.000000', NULL, 0),
