(558771, 54128, 7020, '<td valign="top">I really like what you did with this shot. It''s great.</td>', 'I really like what you did with this shot. It''s great.', '2004-01-27 08:10:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(558846, 54715, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Mhamilton...<br/> <br/>I think this is an excellent composition and study in shapes/contrast.  I think it may also have some strong potential as a black and white because of those elements and the texture of the ice.  As far as point of view is concerned, I don''t think this is a particularly strong image.  The point of view for this photo doesn''t seem to add to the impact of the image.  The contrast and shapes are dominant.  Challenges usually require some fine attention to the challenge topic.  Your approach to the topic should be clear and well-defined.  <br/> <br/>I like it :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Mhamilton... I think this is an excellent composition and study in shapes/contrast.  I think it may also have some strong potential as a black and white because of those elements and the texture of the ice.  As far as point of view is concerned, I don''t think this is a particularly strong image.  The point of view for this photo doesn''t seem to add to the impact of the image.  The contrast and shapes are dominant.  Challenges usually require some fine attention to the challenge topic.  Your approach to the topic should be clear and well-defined.   I like it :) John Setzler', '2004-01-27 10:22:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(558972, 54262, 9411, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Well, it is amusing.  But I''m not sure there are many people that really want to look up another persons nose!<br/> <br/>It''s a good idea, and one that is hard to execute. There is little here that is in focus and the slightly overall washed out colours are not real engaging.<br/> <br/>I''m afraid I don''t have a lot of suggestions on how to improve this image. Possibly some cross lighting to highlight the bottle more.  Maybe creating a DOF that shows more of your face.<br/> <br/>Sorry.  remember just my opinion<br/> <br/>JC</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Well, it is amusing.  But I''m not sure there are many people that really want to look up another persons nose! It''s a good idea, and one that is hard to execute. There is little here that is in focus and the slightly overall washed out colours are not real engaging. I''m afraid I don''t have a lot of suggestions on how to improve this image. Possibly some cross lighting to highlight the bottle more.  Maybe creating a DOF that shows more of your face. Sorry.  remember just my opinion JC', '2004-01-27 12:41:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(559009, 54115, 9964, '<td valign="top">just read your profile :) For an eleven year old I think it''s great that you are entering the challenges. You have a good eye and the technical skill will follow if you stick with it. My advice to you "Stick With It!" Maybe you should try some shots on a tripod and see if you like the results. Good Luck To You!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-01-27 13:18:04.</i></td>', 'just read your profile :) For an eleven year old I think it''s great that you are entering the challenges. You have a good eye and the technical skill will follow if you stick with it. My advice to you "Stick With It!" Maybe you should try some shots on a tripod and see if you like the results. Good Luck To You!', '2004-01-27 13:17:42.000000', '2004-01-27 13:18:04.000000', 0),
(559136, 54918, 5158, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts/My opinion</b> <br/>Great point of view, right on the topic. Took me quiet some time to get what it is though.<br/> <br/><b>Content/Composition</b> <br/>This is of course a very special point of view you have form your apartment! The view to the trees from far above is already very special by itself, but the grave stones just top it. Very good choice.<br/>However, the image is a little confusing: it takes some time to get what one is looking at: first there is the network of the tree branches and then one sees some rectangular bright "thinks". Only at the very top one can see that there are actually grave stones. Then, after reading the title the image becomes of course clear.<br/>A more clear, easier to get portion (maybe just the top) and a tighter crop or more zoomed in would have been better.<br/>As mentioned by others, the image appears to be a little bright/low contrasted. Darkening it would probably improved it a bit.<br/> <br/>You mentioned that the trees should resemble their roots under the grave yard. While I do see the intention, it didn''t work well for me: even if I try to imagine this, my brain switches back to the inverse, real scene. Doesn''t matter much though.<br/> <br/><b>Camera work - Technically</b> <br/>Focus seems fine although the image is a little fuzzy due to the many branches, but this is not important. Exposure see above.<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>You did a good job on sharpening: not too much, just right. <br/>A border might have been nice.<br/> <br/><b>Fits the challenge</b> <br/>Of course, very good!<br/> <br/>Good luck for your upcoming submissions</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Initial thoughts/My opinion Great point of view, right on the topic. Took me quiet some time to get what it is though. Content/Composition This is of course a very special point of view you have form your apartment! The view to the trees from far above is already very special by itself, but the grave stones just top it. Very good choice.However, the image is a little confusing: it takes some time to get what one is looking at: first there is the network of the tree branches and then one sees some rectangular bright "thinks". Only at the very top one can see that there are actually grave stones. Then, after reading the title the image becomes of course clear.A more clear, easier to get portion (maybe just the top) and a tighter crop or more zoomed in would have been better.As mentioned by others, the image appears to be a little bright/low contrasted. Darkening it would probably improved it a bit. You mentioned that the trees should resemble their roots under the grave yard. While I do see the intention, it didn''t work well for me: even if I try to imagine this, my brain switches back to the inverse, real scene. Doesn''t matter much though. Camera work - Technically Focus seems fine although the image is a little fuzzy due to the many branches, but this is not important. Exposure see above. Digital Processing - Technical You did a good job on sharpening: not too much, just right. A border might have been nice. Fits the challenge Of course, very good! Good luck for your upcoming submissions', '2004-01-27 15:29:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(559402, 54926, 16529, '<td valign="top">This is a really cool photo. I like the moral behind the photo. You got a really nice shot of the fire, and I like how you made the cigarettes your main image!<br/> <br/>One thing, the top half of the picture is too dark, it makes too much of a contrast between the bright flame and itself. You might want to enhance that part of the photo. Other than that...great job!<br/> <br/>geschlechtmann27<br/>Critique Club :)</td>', 'This is a really cool photo. I like the moral behind the photo. You got a really nice shot of the fire, and I like how you made the cigarettes your main image! One thing, the top half of the picture is too dark, it makes too much of a contrast between the bright flame and itself. You might want to enhance that part of the photo. Other than that...great job! geschlechtmann27Critique Club :)', '2004-01-27 18:56:19.000000', NULL, 0),
